WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:09.030
Donald Trump, we have now learned, thanks
to Bob Woodward's book Rage, supposedly bragged

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:14.430
about a secret nuclear weapons system when
he was speaking to Bob Woodward during these

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.619
interviews that took place over the last six
months for Bob Woodward's book.

00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:22.710
This is according to excerpts from the book
that have been released.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:29.199
Trump talked openly about a weapons system
with Bob Woodward that is supposed to be secret.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:33.030
And this was in the context of telling Bob
Woodward how close we supposedly were to war

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:38.140
with North Korea nuclear war in 2017, which
is a whole horrifying nightmare in and of

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.140
itself.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.239
And according to the excerpts that The Washington
Post has published, Trump told Bob Woodward,

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:49.530
quote, I have built a nuclear a weapons system
that nobody's ever had in this country before.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.649
We have stuff that you haven't even seen or
heard about.

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:58.809
We have stuff that Putin and Xi have never
heard about before, saying there is nobody.

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:01.100
What we have is incredible.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:07.180
And then in the book, Bob Woodward goes on
to say unnamed sources that he spoke to and

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.180
said, what?

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.219
What is Trump talking about here?

00:01:10.219 --> 00:01:16.229
Sources did confirm the existence of a new
weapons system to Bob Woodward, but they said

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:17.630
they couldn't share any details.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:22.549
And they expressed surprise that Donald Trump
actually mentioned it to Bob Woodward because

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.530
he wasn't supposed to.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.780
The Hill then reached out to the Pentagon
for comment.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.979
The Pentagon said they don't talk about books
that have not yet been published.

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:38.289
And when The Hill did more investigation into
this, they spoke to, for example, James Acton

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:42.789
from the Carnegie Endowment for International
Peace.

00:01:42.789 --> 00:01:51.529
And what James Acton said is this probably
is a submarine launched low yield nuclear

00:01:51.529 --> 00:01:55.759
warhead and its existence is now known.

00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:59.169
But the details remain classified.

00:01:59.169 --> 00:02:00.169
This is so.

00:02:00.169 --> 00:02:01.219
So there's two sides to this.

00:02:01.219 --> 00:02:02.979
One is we shouldn't even have this stuff.

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:05.929
We need nuclear disarmament.

00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:10.689
And maybe Trump spilling the beans will help
build that case.

00:02:10.689 --> 00:02:15.860
The other side is Donald Trump is just so
irresponsible with classified and secret information.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.410
And he criticized Hillary Clinton for that.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:21.620
And he criticizes Adam Schiff and Chuck Schumer
and Nancy Pelosi for that.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:27.829
And yet it's Trump who has the record of bragging
about new weapons that are publicly unknown

00:02:27.829 --> 00:02:31.239
or semi known and disclosing details.

00:02:31.239 --> 00:02:35.170
Remember the thing about the supersonic missile
that goes superduper missile that goes 17

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.900
